---
/**
 * About — static page. Honest description of the product, its current
 * scope, and the roadmap. No invented stats, team, or history.
 */
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What the AI Graphing Calculator is, its current foundation-phase scope, and what's planned next."
  canonicalPath="/about/"
  mainClass="mx-auto w-full max-w-3xl px-4 py-10 sm:py-14"
>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white">About</h1>

  <div class="mt-6 space-y-4 text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
    <p>
      The AI Graphing Calculator is an original, browser-based math tool for graphing functions and
      exploring mathematics. It is an independent implementation — built from scratch, not derived
      from any other graphing product.
    </p>
    <p>
      The project is currently in its foundation phase. What exists today is real and usable:
      expression management (multiple expressions with colors and visibility controls), viewport
      state with zoom and reset, and a saved workspace in your browser. The interactive 2D graph
      renderer is in active development and lands next.
    </p>
    <h2 class="pt-2 text-xl font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Roadmap</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
      <li>
        <strong class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Interactive 2D renderer</strong>—
        zoom, pan, and adaptive grid, then real function plotting.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">AI assistance</strong>—
        natural-language math commands and step-by-step explanations, with the AI assisting
        exploration rather than replacing real calculation.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Tables and sliders</strong>—
        values tables and interactive parameter sliders.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong class="font-medium text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Sharing</strong>— save and share
        graph states via links.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Nothing here is presented as working before it is. When a roadmap item ships, this page will
      say so.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
